#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:2
msgid "Using in-development features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:4
msgid ""
"If you need to use a new feature of ``snapd`` as soon as it is available, "
"but before it is supported by the validation mechanisms in Snapcraft, you "
"have the option of using the passthrough feature of ``snapcraft.yaml`` to "
"specify the in-development feature you need."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:9
msgid "The passthrough keyword"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:11
msgid ""
"Snapcraft can accept the ``passthrough`` keyword in two places in the "
"``snapcraft.yaml`` file. It can be used at the top-level scope to access new "
"top-level features, and also at the application scope to access new "
"application-level features. Where either or these locations are used, they "
"are referred to as the *target scope*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:17
msgid ""
"The ``passthrough`` keyword defines a map whose keywords and values are "
"copied directly into the corresponding scope in the ``snap.yaml`` "
"description that ``snapd`` uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:21
msgid ""
"Although Snapcraft does not know about in-development features, it performs "
"some checks to prevent accidental conflicts or unexpected behaviour as a "
"result of using passthroughs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:25
msgid ""
"It forbids the definition of an option inside a passthrough if that option "
"is also directly present in the target scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:27
msgid ""
"It warns the developer about the options used in each passthrough, to remind "
"the publisher that these options are not yet supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:29
msgid ""
"It may also report options that might already be supported, but it should "
"not prevent these options from being passed through to ``snap.yaml`` since "
"the option may be defined in a way that is not yet understood by Snapcraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:33
msgid ""
"Files using in-development features will need to be updated when those "
"features become supported by Snapcraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:36
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:38
msgid ""
"In the following example, the ``passthrough`` keyword is used at the top-"
"level scope to access two new, *hypothetical*, top-level features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:41
msgid ""
"   name: foo\n"
"   passthrough:\n"
"       confinement: next-generation\n"
"       planet: saturn\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:48
msgid ""
"This example enables the usage of a new value for the existing ``snapcraft-"
"yaml-confinement`` keyword. It also enables an entirely new ``planet`` "
"keyword to be used, along with a new value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:52
msgid ""
"The following example shows the use of the keyword to access a new "
"application-level feature:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:55
msgid ""
"   apps:\n"
"       foo:\n"
"           command: foo\n"
"           passthrough:\n"
"               daemon: complex\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/using-in-development-features.md:63
msgid ""
"In this case, a passthrough is used within the scope of the app ``foo`` to "
"set the existing ``daemon`` keyword to a value of ``complex``."
msgstr ""
